<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Follow</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>follow &lt;character&gt;
follow self
<a cmd='#'>follow</a>
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>follow asta
</pre>
<p>To start following someone, you use this command. Wherever the character you 
follow goes, you go too. You must be following someone, or have someone 
following you, to form a group (see <a cmd='#'>Help Groups</a>).
</p><p>To stop following someone, follow yourself: follow self. follow alone tells you 
who you are following. If someone doesn't want you to follow them, they may 
ditch you (see <a cmd='#'>Help Ditch</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Groups</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Ditch</a>
</pre>




</div>